	(text "NIBBLE CARD CTR7 - COUNTER BIT 7: program counter bit 7 and return register bit 7"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 15.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.5 3.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "6fca2983-fc02-4fb5-9835-386025dcf3d3")
	)
	(text "Cell: 2N7000 + 47k pull-up (NMOS, see docs/gate-cell.md).  59 transistors, 32 resistors, 2 LEDs, 100 x 100 mm (docs/cards.md).\nFrom the bus header: PCE (count), PCL (load the jump target), CLK, RST.   To the bus header: PC7.\nFrom the sequencer over the LINK ribbon (2x6, chained along the eight counter cards): OPR7 (the jump target bit), PCR (load the return address), RAI (save the return address).\nCount carry TC7 in from bit 6 over the IN link; the carry chain ends here.\nPC7: a master-slave flip-flop whose input is PC xor carry (count, or hold when PCE is low), OPR7 (PCL) or RA7 (PCR).  RA7: a transparent latch open while RAI and PH1.  RST clears both.\ndocs/isa.md is the specification; sim/emu.py the reference the whole-machine simulation checks the cards against."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 45.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a460b6bc-0105-4106-bdff-392c05d0d6c4")
	)
	(text "TWO-PHASE CLOCK and RSTN (as on the register and sequencer boards)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 165.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "db71b2ec-01ae-41d4-b668-2d533754c35b")
	)
